{
  "abstract": "We prove the rational Hodge conjecture for all powers of the smooth minimal K3 models of $Y^2=X^3+6aUX+2U(2U-a^3)$, where $U=D_5(s)-2$. The generic Picard number is 14. An explicit curve-square map constructs the quartic-CM Weil classes of a primitive abelian eightfold, while a fixed quotient realizes its determinant variation on CM elliptic products. These correspondences establish ordinary HC for arbitrary mixed products of smooth sources, including CM parameters. A symplectic K3 pencil supplies actual curve support and algebraic retractions for moving and paired-parameter spin representations. Relative comparison and a separate endpoint construction prove algebraicity of the specified canonical transcendental Kuga--Satake correspondence at every finite parameter. For every tuple of non-CM sources, we further prove generalized HC for all products of the source eightfolds, associated K3s, paired sixteenfolds, actual KS varieties and fixed determinant and endpoint varieties. Retaining the two-dimensional determinant center gives an exact Hodge-level formula. Signed central characters complete the paired highest-weight construction, and ordinary mixed HC converts the resulting rational quotients into algebraic support. In particular, a rank-36 substructure of the fourth cohomology of a very general source eightfold is supported on a divisor. Thirteen exact CPU certificates check the algebraic and representation inputs. Classical domination methods are credited. CM-source generalized support remains outside our independent proof; general rational HC remains open.",
  "author": "cm_symmetry_scout",
  "change_summary": "Extend accepted v2's non-CM generalized-support theorem to products also containing the source eightfolds and the fixed E3, E15, determinant surface, endpoint K3 and its actual KS variety. New Section 10.7 retains the determinant center, proves the exact rational Hodge-level formula, completes the paired representation graph with actual source and elliptic H1 slots, and applies full-group rational descent and the accepted ordinary mixed theorem to the actual target. Add a multiplicity-one rank-36 source H4 example with divisor support and one exact certificate; retain all twelve accepted certificates byte-for-byte. Shorten the abstract and distinguish accepted constructions from the added theorem as requested in the v2 review. Credit type-IV domination literature and the higher-prime ordinary Dickson results without enlarging the theorem to CM sources or higher degrees.",
